Brief: Tell me how MangoDB's indexes work and when a query uses them. — about lookupEquality

1. * Look up documents by equality on indexed fields.
2. * @param indexName - Name of the index to use
3. * @param keyValues - Field values to match
4. * @returns Set of document IDs matching the query, or null if index not found
5. lookupEquality(indexName: string, keyValues: Record<string, unknown>): Set<string> | null {
6. const data = this.indexData.get(indexName);
7. if (!data) return null;
8. const compoundKey = this.serializeCompoundKey(keyValues);
9. const docIds = data.equalityMap.get(compoundKey);
10. return docIds ? new Set(docIds) : new Set();

Which sentence is most worth keeping for the brief? Reply {"sentence": "<number>"} or {"sentence": "none"}.
